---
import PageMasthead from '../components/PageMasthead.astro'
import FeedbackForm from '../components/FeedbackForm.astro'
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from '../lib/site'
import { href } from '../lib/url'

const description =
  "St. Louing is an independent guide to the food and neighborhoods of St. Louis. It's a love letter to an underrated city, built in the spirit of the early internet."
---

<BaseLayout crumb="About" title={`About ${SITE_NAME}`} description={description}>
  <article>
    <PageMasthead title="About">
      <p slot="lede">My ongoing project to document St. Louis</p>
    </PageMasthead>

    <div class="body reading-col">
      <img class="emblem" src="/logo-outlined.svg" alt="St. Louing logo" width="120" height="156" />

      <p>
        Welcome! St. Louing is a personal project I created to document my experience living in St.
        Louis and learning to love it.
      </p>

      <p>
        I've been on a quest to find <a href={href('/food/')}>the best food in St. Louis</a>, and
        after realizing I've tried more
        <a
          class="wikilink"
          data-wikilink="st-louis-style-pizza"
          href={href('/st-louis-style-pizza/')}>St. Louis-style pizza</a
        >
        than anyone I know, I thought a website would be a fun way to share everything I've discovered.
      </p>

      <p>All photography on this site was taken in person, by me, in St. Louis.</p>

      <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>

      <p>
        Follow at <a href="https://instagram.com/st.louing">st.louing</a> or email me at <a
          href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a
        > or fill out the form.
      </p>

      <FeedbackForm subject="feedback" />

      <h2 id="uses">Uses</h2>

      <p>A few open-source projects this site relies on.</p>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Host</strong> - <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/pages">Github Pages</a>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Web Framework</strong> - <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a></li>
        <li>
          <strong>Maps</strong> - <a href="https://maplibre.org">MapLibre GL</a> /
          <a href="https://protomaps.com">Protomaps</a> /
          <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a>
          <ul>
            <li>
              Map vector files for St. Louis greater area were saved as a <code>.pmtiles</code>
              binary and served from <a href="https://supabase.com/">Supabase</a> to prevent relying on
              third-party CDNs.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li><strong>Icons</strong> - <a href="https://tabler.io/icons">Tabler Icons</a></li>
        <li><strong>Forms</strong> - <a href="https://formspree.io">Formspree</a></li>
        <li>
          <strong>Analytics</strong> - <a href="https://www.goatcounter.com">GoatCounter</a>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="links">Links</h2>

      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.builtstlouis.net"><strong>Built St. Louis</strong></a>
          <ul>
            <li>
              A website documenting the historic architecture of St. Louis in the "old internet"
              style of website I love to see.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://stlurbanists.org/"><strong>STL Urbanists</strong></a>
          <ul>
            <li>
              A grassroots advocacy group working to create safer and more effective infrastructure
              for pedestrians, bicycle users, and transit riders.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.stlouiscitytalk.com/"><strong>St. Louis City Talk</strong></a>
          <ul>
            <li>Many thoughts and pictures about St. Louis neighborhoods.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://nextstl.com/"><strong>Next STL</strong></a>
          <ul>
            <li>A website covering civic engagement and development in St. Louis.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.stlmag.com/"><strong>St. Louis Magazine</strong></a>
          <ul>
            <li>STL-based magazine with news and events.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.stlpr.org/"><strong>St. Louis Public Radio</strong></a>
          <ul>
            <li>The St. Louis branch of the NPR network.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.instagram.com/pizzababble"><strong>pizzababble</strong></a>
          <ul>
            <li>
              The St. Louis pizza guy. He's out here fighting the good fight. I've discovered some
              new places thanks to his feed.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/STLFood"><strong>STLFood on Reddit</strong></a>
          <ul>
            <li>The place to discuss food in St. Louis.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://www.stlouis-mo.gov/"><strong>St. Louis-MO.gov</strong></a>
          <ul>
            <li>Used for determining neighborhood boundaries and facts.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href="https://stlouispatina.com/"><strong>St. Louis Patina</strong></a>
          <ul>
            <li>A blog detailing the beauty of St. Louis architecture.</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="etymology">Etymology</h2>

      <p>
        The name <em>St. Louing</em> is meant to represent the ongoing nature of my journey. I know it
        sounds a little cheugy, but let's just roll with it.
      </p>

      <h2 id="history">History</h2>

      <p>This site began on May 28, 2026. My St. Louis experience began in 2023.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
